    "note": "Sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack zoology section (book p.45, SAQ 50). Zoology holds only ONE source book — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no zoology board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the back-test are both structurally impossible for this card; 'not checked' does NOT mean 'checked and clean'. The mark split is a claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. APPEARANCES: the book prints [AP, TS M-16], [AP-18], [TS M-19] and [AP MAY-17,19]; the last two citations are printed to the right of the diagram on the same question block and are read here as belonging to this question. TEXT BEYOND THE BOOK: the book prints the labelled figure alone with no written answer; the naming lines are authored from the labels the book itself prints. FIGURE SCOPE: the book prints a shaded ventral view; this card draws the same view simplified — labrum, the pair of mandibles, the pair of maxillae with cardo, stipes, galea, lacinia and maxillary palp, the labium with submentum, mentum, prementum, glossa, paraglossa and labial palp, and the hypopharynx in the middle. The book labels 16 pieces; this figure draws 14 — PALPIFER and PALPIGER (the small segments that carry the maxillary and labial palps) are deliberately not drawn, because at exam scale they crowd the palp bases. A teacher who needs all 16 marked can add them at the palp bases."
