        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Parts",
        "lines": [
          "The mouthparts of the cockroach are of the",
          "biting and chewing type.",
          "They are the labrum, one pair of mandibles,",
          "one pair of maxillae, the labium and the",
          "hypopharynx.",
          "The space they enclose in front of the mouth",
          "is the pre-oral cavity."
        ],
        "why": "Five names in a fixed order, front to back, tell the examiner what the drawing will show and stop the paired pieces being drawn singly.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing one mandible and one maxilla. Both are PAIRED; the labrum, labium and hypopharynx are single.",
          "Calling the mouthparts the sucking type. The cockroach bites and chews."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Front to back: upper lip, jaws, second jaws, lower lip, and the tongue in the middle.",
        "margin_note": "Type of mouthparts, then the five names in order. Three short lines are enough."
