        "why": "The figure is drawn as a symmetrical spread: the single pieces sit on the middle line and the paired pieces sit outside them, so the position of a piece in the drawing already tells the student which name it takes.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the labium above and the labrum below. The labrum is the UPPER lip and is drawn at the top.",
          "Leaving the hypopharynx out. It is the middle piece between the maxillae.",
          "Giving the maxilla and the labium the same palp name. One is the maxillary palp, the other the labial palp."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw the middle line first: labrum at the top, hypopharynx in the middle, labium at the bottom. Then add the mandibles and maxillae as matching pairs on both sides.",
        "margin_note": "Both marks are in the labels — labrum, mandible, hypopharynx, galea, lacinia, maxillary palp, glossa, paraglossa, labial palp."
